# Visible copy: no AI tells

Applies to **user-facing** site strings: UI text, headlines, body copy, CTAs, alt text, aria labels, form placeholders, catalogue intros, and data in `lib/data/` that renders on the page.

Does **not** apply to: code comments, docs (`docs/`), metadata / `<title>` / Open Graph / tab names, commit messages, or internal TODOs.

## Never use in visible copy

- Em dashes (`—`) or en dashes (`–`). Use a period, comma, colon, or ASCII hyphen (`-`) instead.
- Fancy ellipsis (`…`). Use `...` only if needed, or rephrase.
- Stock AI phrasing: "seamless", "elevate", "unlock", "leverage", "cutting-edge", "robust solution", "delve", "empower", "transform your", "in today's world", "when it comes to", "it's important to note", "without the fluff", "game-changer", etc.
- Meta / process voice aimed at the visitor: "placeholder", "coming soon once confirmed", "will appear here when…", "pending client deliverables".

## Tone

- Straight, technical, B2B. Specs and brand names over marketing cadence.
- Short sentences. Prefer facts the buyer can act on.
- Do not invent company claims, years in business, or certifications.

## Examples

```text
❌ Hydraulic Pumps — Yuken, Rexroth, Vickers
✅ Hydraulic Pumps: Yuken, Rexroth, Vickers

❌ Specs, brands, and local support — without the marketing fluff.
✅ Specs, brands, and local support for plant and OEM buyers.

❌ Contact details and a fuller story will appear here once confirmed.
✅ Browse by category and make, then request a quote.
```

When editing existing copy, strip these patterns if you touch the string. Do not reintroduce them.
